-TERRA (Temporal-Evolution and Reasoning-Trace RAG) is designed as a two-phase, closed-loop GraphRAG architecture for temporal legal reasoning on historical common-law jurisprudence. The core engineering philosophy strictly separates offline corpus ingestion and knowledge structure construction from online query routing and inference. This separation ensures that all computationally intensive graph traversals, citation link extractions, and reasoning trace generations are performed offline, maintaining responsive online inference with a bimodal latency profile (median \TerraFastPathMedianSeconds~s on factual lookups vs. \TerraHardPathMedianSeconds~s on multi-hop citation chains; Figure~\ref{fig:system_architecture}).
+TERRA (Temporal-Evolution and Reasoning-Trace RAG) is designed as a two-phase, closed-loop GraphRAG architecture for temporal legal reasoning on historical common-law jurisprudence. The core engineering philosophy strictly separates offline corpus ingestion and knowledge structure construction from online query routing and inference. Citation extraction, procedural-scaffold construction and indexing are performed offline; retrieval, HARD-route graph traversal, entailment grading and generation are online operations. The evaluated Category~A and Category~B queries have different latency profiles (median \TerraFastPathMedianSeconds~s on factual lookups vs. \TerraHardPathMedianSeconds~s on multi-hop citation chains; Figure~\ref{fig:system_architecture}).
 
 
